---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Hostbox — Deploy to your own VM">
  <section class="site-container hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <span class="eyebrow">Open-source deployment platform</span>
      <h1 class="display">Your code.<br/><span class="word-accent">Your server.</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">The polished git-to-production workflow you expect, running entirely on infrastructure you control.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/VatsalP117/hostbox/blob/main/docs/SELF-HOSTING.md">Deploy Hostbox <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="button" href="https://github.com/VatsalP117/hostbox">View on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="product-window" aria-label="Hostbox dashboard preview">
    <div class="product-bar"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" style="width:16px;height:16px;color:#52a8ff"><path d="M6.5 10.5 16 5l9.5 5.5v11L16 27l-9.5-5.5v-11Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="m6.5 10.5 9.5 5.5 9.5-5.5M16 16v11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><strong>Hostbox</strong><span>/</span><span>Projects</span><span style="margin-left:auto">⌘ K</span></div>
    <div class="product-body">
      <aside class="product-nav"><span class="active">Overview</span><span>Projects</span><span>Deployments</span><span>Domains</span><span>Environment</span><span>System</span></aside>
      <div class="product-main">
        <div class="product-heading"><div><strong style="font-size:18px">Projects</strong><div style="margin-top:5px;color:#777;font-size:12px">Everything running on your VM</div></div><span class="button button-primary" style="min-height:34px;padding-inline:14px">Add project</span></div>
        <div class="project-grid">
          <div class="project"><strong>web-app</strong><p>app.example.com</p><small><i class="status-dot"></i>Ready · main · 42s ago</small></div>
          <div class="project"><strong>docs</strong><p>docs.example.com</p><small><i class="status-dot"></i>Ready · main · 3m ago</small></div>
          <div class="project"><strong>api</strong><p>api.example.com</p><small><i class="status-dot"></i>Ready · production · 9m ago</small></div>
          <div class="project"><strong>storefront</strong><p>shop.example.com</p><small><i class="status-dot" style="background:#f5a623"></i>Building · feature/cart</small></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section site-container">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">A familiar workflow</span><h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:20px">From git push to a live URL.</h2></div>
      <p class="section-copy">Connect a repository once. Hostbox detects your framework, builds in isolation, routes traffic, provisions TLS, and keeps every deployment ready to roll back.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-grid">
      <article class="panel panel-wide"><span class="panel-label">01 / DEPLOY</span><div class="panel-visual"><span class="flow-node">git push</span><span class="flow-line"></span><span class="flow-node">build</span><span class="flow-line"></span><span class="flow-node">live</span></div><h3>Zero-config when you want it.</h3><p>Automatic framework detection with explicit build settings available whenever your project needs them.</p></article>
      <article class="panel"><span class="panel-label">02 / DOMAINS</span><div class="panel-visual"><span style="font-size:44px">◎</span></div><h3>HTTPS, automatically.</h3><p>Add a domain. Hostbox configures routing and lets Caddy provision and renew the certificate.</p></article>
      <article class="panel"><span class="panel-label">03 / PREVIEWS</span><div class="panel-visual"><span class="flow-node">feature/login</span></div><h3>Preview every change.</h3><p>Branch deployments give changes a production-like URL before they reach your users.</p></article>
      <article class="panel"><span class="panel-label">04 / SECRETS</span><div class="panel-visual"><code style="color:#777">API_KEY=••••••••</code></div><h3>Encrypted variables.</h3><p>Environment values are encrypted at rest and scoped to the projects that need them.</p></article>
      <article class="panel"><span class="panel-label">05 / ROLLBACK</span><div class="panel-visual"><span style="font-size:42px">↶</span></div><h3>Back to healthy, fast.</h3><p>Immutable build artifacts make prior deployments available for immediate rollback.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section site-container site-rule">
    <div class="section-heading"><h2 class="section-title">Small footprint.<br/>Full control.</h2><p class="section-copy">Hostbox is a Go service, a React dashboard, and infrastructure primitives you can inspect. No per-seat pricing. No proprietary runtime.</p></div>
    <div class="metric-row"><div class="metric"><strong>~200MB</strong><span>Typical idle memory</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>1 VM</strong><span>Minimum infrastructure</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>0</strong><span>Platform markups</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>MIT</strong><span>Open-source license</span></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta"><h2 class="section-title" style="margin-inline:auto">Your next deployment can be yours.</h2><p class="section-copy">Install Hostbox on a VM, connect GitHub, and ship your first project.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/VatsalP117/hostbox/blob/main/docs/SELF-HOSTING.md">Read the self-hosting guide</a><a class="button" href="/features">Explore the platform</a></div></section>
</Layout>
